{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1203980-habbiti-ma-and-the-hototogisu-in-hunter-2ed","id":1203980,"title":"Habbiti Ma and The Hototogisu in Hunter 2ed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-06T14:04:42-07:00","id":1203980,"title":"Habbiti Ma and The Hototogisu in Hunter 2ed","content":"I think Habibti Ma and the Hototogisu should be part of the Hunter 2ed Core Compacts &amp; Conspiracies.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhy, you may be asking do I think so? Well, for Habibti Ma, it's because of their sheer versatility:<br /> <br /> \u200bI know they were created as a Compact that would oppose Mummies (mainly their cults), but think about it like this: Most splats in the Chronicles of Darkness can have Cults or cult-like groups!<br /> <br /> \u200bVampire blood cults, Mage mystery cults (especially either Seer or Guardian ones), Werewolf spirit cults (*cough*<i>Les Mysteres</i>*cough*), Changeling developed cults of personality, Sin-Eater Krewes, Cults of the God Machine, and Beast Primordial Cults. Habibti Ma could wind up battling the forces of any number of supernatural forces, not just Mummies.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs for the Hototogisu... <i>COME ON PEOPLE!</i>\u200b They found a way to acquire Dread Powers without any sort of strings or side effects on their part, they control the Vampire covens of Tokyo, and considering how all the 2ed core books mention Tokyo, I think it would be pretty odd not to give them an entry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T14:30:11-07:00","id":1203987,"title":"","content":"Don't they get their power through ghastly cannibalism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T14:32:13-07:00","id":1203989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1203980-habbiti-ma-and-the-hototogisu-in-hunter-2ed?p=1203987#post1203987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't they get their power through ghastly cannibalism?</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s the Faithful of Shulpae, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T14:33:54-07:00","id":1203991,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah. How do these guys power work? But I do agree a group of cult hunters is very versatile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T14:38:45-07:00","id":1203993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1203980-habbiti-ma-and-the-hototogisu-in-hunter-2ed?p=1203991#post1203991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah. How do these guys power work? But I do agree a group of cult hunters is very versatile.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHototogisu effective buy their powers off of monsters. Unlike Shulpae, who get sick if they eat more then their stamina (because the human body was never meant to process raw monster flesh), Hototogisu's Setto has not drawbacks or strings attached; if you can convince the monster to sell it to you, that power is yours! ...Though you can only have up to 5 powers total (like Lucifuge's Castigation).<br /> <br /> And yeah, the Faithful of Shulpae are gross.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T14:47:27-07:00","id":1203997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1203980-habbiti-ma-and-the-hototogisu-in-hunter-2ed?p=1203991#post1203991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah. How do these guys power work? But I do agree a group of cult hunters is very versatile.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAlso, if you want more info on Hototogisu, check out either Dark Eras: <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/178583/Chronicles-of-Darkness-Dark-Eras?src=hottest_filtered\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/...ttest_filtered</a><br /> <br /> <br /> or (for the budget conscious) Dark Eras: Fallen Blossoms: <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/205483/Dark-Eras-Fallen-Blossoms-Hunter-the-Vigil?src=hottest_filtered\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/...ttest_filtered</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T14:48:42-07:00","id":1203999,"title":"","content":"Okay I haven't read my copy yet so behind hoho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T17:15:05-07:00","id":1204341,"title":"","content":"The core compacts were designed around showcasing attitudes to the Vigil (thrill-seeking, trying to understand scientifically, trying to publicise, neighbourhood protection, religious duty, with one mixing dusty scholarship with penitence). Habibti Ma fit into this well, given they have a focus on victims over monsters.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't be surprised to see Hototogisu as a main antagonist in either Deviant or the Contagion Chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T18:43:26-07:00","id":1204378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\">